Message-ID: <a9CaFpjWQxC-VwS5HrOdQw@geopod-ismtpd-0>

Hello R-SIG-GENETICS members

A reminder - Careful validation helps researchers interpret model behaviour when observations differ from training data. Data-Driven Methods for Deploying AI is a seminar livestreaming November 6 with Manish Chauhan (School of Physics, Engineering and Technology, University of York). Uncertainty quantification and Bayesian estimation provide tools for evaluating AI systems under sparse or corrupted observations. Researchers in genetic data analysis can use the seminar's diagnostic reasoning to consider how differences between training assumptions and observed conditions affect deployment. A case study compares simulated data streams with real-world sensor noise.

Details and registration: https://instats.org/seminar/data-driven-methods-for-deploying-ai-1
The seminar page includes the full schedule and registration details.


Best wishes

